column6:
The DILG, in collaboration and coordination with other member agencies of the Justice Sector Coordinating Council (JSCC), cognizant to the roles of Barangay Tanods for the swift and fair administration of justice, finds the need to undertake strategic interventions to boost their capability in the performance of their duties with expertise, commitment and integrity. This is in consonance with the duties of barangay tanods as the “frontliners” in the maintenance of peace and order, protection and security of life and property and the maintenance of a desirable environment in their respective barangays. In view of the implementation of the Supreme Court Ruling on the Mandanas-Garcia Petitions and with the additional funds to be provided to LGUs, it is necessary to re-engineer the delivery methodology in providing capacity development interventions to the barangays. To achieve the objectives of this Project, the following strategies shall be implemented:
• Develop all necessary training modules for strengthening capacities of Barangay Tanods; 
• Formulate/update policies on Barangay Tanods; 
• Build a pool of trainers on Barangay Tanod Skills Enhancement to meet the demand of LGUs; and 
• Advocate for the City and Municipality’s provision of relevant trainings for Barangay Tanods within their areas of jurisdiction

The project shall involve the construction of 17 modern and fully equipped fire station buildings with offices, living quarters, training facilities, and vehicle bays, to wit:

•        2 City Fire Stations for Bislig and Tandag Cities in Surigao del Sur;
•        2 Municipal Fire Stations for the Municipalities in Magallanes and Jabonga in Agusan del Norte;
•        4 Municipal Fire Stations for the Municipalities of Esperanza, Trento, Sta. Josefa, and San Francisco in Agusan del Sur;
•        5 Municipal Fire Stations for the Municipalities of Bacuag, Alegria, Del Carmen, Pilar, and San Benito in Surigao del Norte;
•        3 Municipal Fire Stations for the Municipalities of Lingig, Cagwait, and Lanuza in Surigao del Sur; and
•        1 Municipal Fire Station for the Municipality of San Jose in Dinagat Islands.

This is an extension project of USTP Balubal to promote peace and education in the hinterland of Northern Mindanao. The project has the following components:

1. Literacy and peace education for the youth;
2. Peace advocacy Training and Networking;
3. Community service and care for environment; and
4. Digital farm planning for improved sustainable Agricultural production.
